From 84b4f71f14f8f34e4b36172de9a1e8d7dbda78f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DongDongJu <commisori28@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:32:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Validate KV-event request namespaces before EngineCore
 enqueue

Add a class-level connector admission hook gated on enabled KV events, with
MultiConnector forwarding and a default no-op for existing connectors. Apply
it to both processed inputs and prepared requests so invalid namespaces can
raise a per-request VLLMValidationError without terminating EngineCore.

Validated with 79 focused frontend/connector tests and pre-commit. A pinned
vLLM 0.31.0 API probe confirmed HTTP 400 plus healthy subsequent inference
for an unsupported namespace, through direct and MultiConnector paths;
events-disabled inference still accepts the same request.

Co-authored-by: Dongjoo Seo <dongjoo.seo1@samsung.com>
Signed-off-by: DongDongJu <commisori28@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Dongjoo Seo <dongjoo.seo1@samsung.com>
